  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 141 PM MDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nPotential day-2 severe set-up on the plains Sunday, as post\nfrontal upslope deepens under brisk w-sw flow aloft, while\nstrong upper trough lifts out of WY into the High Plains. CAPE\n1k-2k J/KG and 0-6km shear over 30 kts (localized 40-50 kts\nbetween KCOS and KLIC) look favorable for strong/severe storms,\nespecially with dynamic lift from the upper trough passing over\nthe region. Storms likely initiate along the Palmer Divide \nmid/late afternoon, spreading southeast onto the plains through \nthe evening. NBM pops looked ok for the most part, but did trim \nback numbers some, especially along the Wets/srn I-25 corridor, \nwhere forcing looks weaker. Models suggest weakening activity\ncould even persist into Mon morning, though QPF by then will be\nrather light. \n\nFor next week, trend would appear to be toward wetter\nconditions once again, with upper high over TX and general \ntroughing along the West Coast. Still a good deal of\nvariance among the models/ensembles regarding timing/strength on\ns/w troughs and associated moisture surges, so forecast\nconfidence is moderate at this point. Currently thinking is Mon\nmay end up the driest day, at least over mountains, with \nscattered storms still possible on the plains. Wettest days \ncould be Tue and again Thu, with srn mountains (ern San \nJuans/srn Sangres) most favored for rainfall. Temps will likely \nstay within a few degf of seasonal averages through the period.",
